<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90668" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προφερής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προφέρω</span>) poet. Adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>carried before, placed before,
				excelling</i>, c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλάων προφερής τ᾽ ἦν πρεσβυτάτη τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					260
				</span></i>
			: <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only 
				Comp.
			 (exc. 
				Sup.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλματι . . πάντων προφερέστατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					8.128
				</span></i>
			), <i>more excellent</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν δ᾽ ἄλλων ἐμέ φημι πολὺ
					προφερέστερον εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					8.221
				</span></i>
			: c. dat. rei, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίῃ προφερέστερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					21.134
				</span></i>
			: c. inf., [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμίονοι] βοῶν προφερέστεραί εἰσιν
					ἑλκέμεναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.352
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προφερεστάτη ἐστὶν ἁπασέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					79
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				361
			</span></i> (where it is commonly interpreted <i>eldest</i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὴρ προφερέστατος ἀνδρῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.935
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				17.4
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡνιόχων π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.1628
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				435
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Trachonitis</span>); also 
				Comp.
			 and 
				Sup.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προφέρτερος,
			προφέρτατος</span> in the sense of <i>older, eldest</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				447
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OC</u>
				1531
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>looking older than one is, well-grown</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Euthd.</u>
				271b
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.49
			</span></i>; of plants and young persons, <i>forced, premature,
				precocious</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Aristox.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.37.4
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>VP</u>
				31.209
			</span></i>.</div>
